# CardForge/MyManaBox - Cursor AI Rules

You are working on CardForge, a professional MTG collection management platform.

## Project Context
- Python 3.9+ with PyQt6 GUI (transitioning from tkinter)
- Windows 11 primary, cross-platform compatible
- SQLite + FTS5 for search
- Scryfall API integration (10 req/sec limit)
- Claude MCP server for AI features

## Key Reference Documents
Before implementing features, check these files:
- `PYQT6_BUILD_SPECIFICATION.md` - GUI implementation spec
- `MTG_COLLECTION_MANAGER_DESIGN_PATTERN.md` - Architecture
- `docs/PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md` - Codebase organization

## Code Style
- Use type hints on all functions
- Use pathlib for file paths (no hardcoded strings)
- Async/await for I/O operations
- Follow existing patterns in src/

## GUI Theme (REQUIRED)
```python
BG_PRIMARY = "#1e1e1e"
BG_SECONDARY = "#252526"
ACCENT_PRIMARY = "#5a4fcf"
TEXT_PRIMARY = "#cccccc"
```

## Testing
- Target 80% coverage
- Test files: `test_<module>.py`
- Functions: `test_<func>_<scenario>()`

## DO NOT
- Block main thread with I/O
- Skip error handling
- Hard-code file paths
- Ignore Scryfall rate limits
- Modify user data without backup

## Architecture
```
src/
├── models/      # Card, Collection, Deck
├── data/        # CSV, Database, API clients
├── services/    # Business logic
├── presentation/# CLI, GUI
└── mcp/         # Claude integration
```
